  "question": {
    "text": "The solubility order for alkali metal fluoride in water is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{LiF} < \\mathrm{RbF} < \\mathrm{KF} < \\mathrm{NaF}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{RbF} < \\mathrm{KF} < \\mathrm{NaF} < \\mathrm{LiF}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{LiF}>\\mathrm{NaF}>\\mathrm{KF}>\\mathrm{RbF}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{LiF} < \\mathrm{NaF} < \\mathrm{KF} < \\mathrm{RbF}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Higher the lattice enthalpy lower will be solubilityi.e., lattice enthalpy $\\propto \\frac{1}{\\text { Solubility }}$\nSince the lattice enthalpy of alkali metals follow the order $\\mathrm{Li}>\\mathrm{Na}>\\mathrm{K}>\\mathrm{Rb}$ Hence the correct order of solubility is $\\mathrm{LiF} < \\mathrm{NaF} < \\mathrm{KF} < \\mathrm{RbF}$"
  }
}